msgstr "Trajectory・Protonation ファイルの準備、PLUMED 入力の生成、出力データの取得用スクリプトもあります。"

#: README.md:31
msgid "Introduction to CpH-Metadynamics"
msgstr "CpH-Metadynamics の導入"

#: README.md:33
msgid ""
"Constant pH Metadynamics is a methodological approach that integrates two "
"main ideas: the [stochastic titration Constant pH Molecular "
"Dynamics](https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1497164) method and the "
"[metadynamics](https://doi.org/10.1038/s42254-020-0153-0) method. For a more"
" detailed explanation of how both these methods work, we recommend a deeper "
"dive into the provided links. However, here we will tackle the main "
"rationale behind the [CpH-Metadynamics "
"approach](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2410.16064) and to do that we will tackle "
"the st-CpHMD first."
msgstr ""
"Constant pH Metadynamics は、[Stochastic Titration Constant pH Molecular "
"Dynamics](https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1497164) と "
"[Metadynamics](https://doi.org/10.1038/s42254-020-0153-0) "
"を統合します。詳細はリンク先を参照してください。ここでは [CpH-"
"Metadynamics](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2410.16064) の基本的な考え方を扱い、まず st-CpHMD "
"を説明します。"

#: README.md:35
msgid "st-CpHMD:"
msgstr "st-CpHMD："

#: README.md:37
msgid ""
"The [st-CpHMD method](https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1497164) and other CpHMD "
"methods aim to introduce an additional parameter into MD simulations which "
"is the pH. The introduction of the pH relates to the fact that the standard "
"MD protocols assume fixed protonation states in their residues whereas, in "
"biological conditions, residue titration is dependent on the pH and the "
"surrounding environment. While there are many valid ways to integrate the "
"chemical potential within MD, in this work we use a start-stop approach to "
"change the protonation state along the simulation partitioned into three "
"main steps:"
msgstr ""
"[st-CpHMD](https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1497164) などは、MD に pH を導入します。通常 MD は残基の "
"Protonation State を固定しますが、生体内では pH と環境に依存して Titration が起きます。Chemical "
"Potential の導入法は複数ありますが、ここでは3段階の Start-stop 法で状態を変えます。"

#: README.md:39
msgid "a Poisson-Boltzmann/Monte Carlo (PB/MC) step ;"
msgstr "Poisson-Boltzmann/Monte Carlo (PB/MC)。"

#: README.md:40
msgid "a solvent relaxation step ;"
msgstr "溶媒の Relaxation。"

#: README.md:41
msgid "a MD production step ;"
msgstr "MD 本計算。"

#: README.md:43
msgid ""
"in the PB/MC, protonation free energies are calculated in a single "
"conformation to determine the likelihood of the different protonation states"
" of a titrable site, which are then sampled through a MC procedure until it "
"satisfies a criterion. Upon reassigning the protonation state, a short MD is"
" run with restraints on the solute to allow the solvent to readjust to the "
"new charges. Finally, there is the production MD step, typically 20 ps, "
"which samples the conformational space. After this step, we reinitiate the "
"cycle for how many times are necessary until we reach the desired simulation"
" length. A deeper dive on how we can extract energies from protonation-"
"dependent properties will be addressed on the analysis segment.This method "
"effectively couples discrete protonation states and conformational sampling,"
" thus allowing a more rich description of a biological system."
msgstr ""
"PB/MC では単一 Conformation で Protonation 自由エネルギーを求め、各状態の確率を計算し、基準を満たすまで MC "
"Sampling します。状態を再割り当てした後、Solute を拘束した短い MD で溶媒を新しい電荷に適応させます。最後に通常20 ps の本計算で"
" Conformation 空間を Sampling します。目的の長さまで Cycle を繰り返します。Protonation "
"依存の性質からのエネルギー抽出は解析編で扱います。離散的な Protonation State と Conformation Sampling "
"を結び付け、生物系をより豊かに記述します。"

#: README.md:45
msgid "Metadynamics integration:"
msgstr "Metadynamics の統合："

#: README.md:47
msgid ""
"In typical metadynamics simulations, specific degrees of freedom are "
"selected as fundamental for a given biological system. Hence, we accelerate "
"the conformational sampling of the system in the function of those degrees "
"of freedom called collective variables (CV) by periodically building a "
"history-dependent bias potential. This bias potential is generated by "
"summing Gaussians along the simulation in the CV space. For more details, "
"check the theory behind the [PLUMED "
"tutorial](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-doc/html/advanced-"
"methods.html) on metadynamics."
msgstr ""
"通常の Metadynamics は、重要な自由度を Collective Variables (CVs) として選び、履歴依存 "
"BiasPotential を周期的に構築して Conformation Sampling を加速します。CV 空間に Gaussian "
"を足し合わせて生成します。理論の詳細は [PLUMED Tutorial](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/advanced-methods.html) を参照してください。"

#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"Effectively, certain degrees of freedom are more challenging to sample and "
"can relate to important conformational properties of the system of interest."
" Furthermore, these degrees of freedom may be regulated by key pH-sensitive "
"residues or certain conformational ensembles require major conformational "
"transitions triggered by changes in the electrostatic environment. These "
"slow degrees of freedom benefit from enhanced sampling techniques such as "
"metadynamics and a CpHMD method that easily changes the protonation state of"
" key residues. This is done by allowing the PLUMED module to be ran in the "
"MD production step of the st-CpHMD method following a pre-defined PLUMED "
"input file with chosen CVs. We will explore how to define these settings in "
"the following section. Integrating PLUMED within the st-CpHMD methodology "
"effectively improves the accuracy of average protonation and pKa "
"calculations as the tutorial will show in later sections."
msgstr ""
"Sampling しにくい自由度は重要な Conformation 特性に関わり、pH "
"感受性残基に制御される場合や、静電環境の変化が大きな遷移を引き起こす場合があります。これらの遅い自由度には Metadynamics と、重要残基の "
"Protonation を容易に変える CpHMD が有用です。選んだ CV の PLUMED 入力に従い、st-CpHMD の本計算中に PLUMED"
" を動かします。設定は次節で扱います。後の解析で示すように、統合により平均 Protonation と pKa の精度が向上します。"

#: README.md:51
msgid "Preparing a CpH-compatible system: an RNA nucleoside"
msgstr "CpH 対応の系の準備：RNA Nucleoside"

#: README.md:53
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we are going to prepare a simple nucleoside system. "
"Uridine is one of the four canonical RNA nucleosides with an experimental "
"pKa of 9.22 "
"[1](https://www.degruyter.com/document/doi/10.1515/znb-1968-0105/html). "
"Despite being a simple system, it will initiate into conformational and "
"protonation dynamics of nucleic acids. The chosen CVs are the $\\chi$ angle "
"and the sugar puckering."
msgstr ""
"単純な Nucleoside、Uridine を準備します。標準 RNA Nucleoside 4種の1つで、実験 pKa は9.22です "
"[1](https://www.degruyter.com/document/doi/10.1515/znb-1968-0105/html)。単純ですが、核酸の"
" Conformation・Protonation Dynamics の入門になります。CV は $\\chi$ 角と Sugar Puckering "
"です。"

#: README.md:57
msgid "<em>Representation of uridine syn state.</em>"
msgstr "<em>Uridine の syn 状態。</em>"

#: README.md:62
msgid "<em>Representation of uridine anti state.</em>"
msgstr "<em>Uridine の anti 状態。</em>"

#: README.md:65
msgid ""
"The $\\chi$ angle is a torsion defined by the O4'-C1'-N1-C2 for the uridine "
"and it orients the relative position of the base to the ribose. There are "
"two main states associated with the base-flipping: the syn state (-90º to "
"90º) and the anti state (90° to +180°; –90° to –180°). Considering the "
"position of the titrable N3, when the moiety is facing the ribose is in the "
"syn state and when facing the solvent is in the anti state."
msgstr ""
"$\\chi$ は Uridine の O4'-C1'-N1-C2 の Torsion で、塩基と Ribose の相対配向を決めます。Base-"
"flipping の主要状態は syn（-90º〜90º）と anti（90°〜+180°、–90°〜–180°）です。Titration する N3 "
"が Ribose を向くと syn、溶媒を向くと anti です。"

#: README.md:67
msgid ""
"The other CV choice relates to sugar puckering. In RNA, the sugar puckering "
"defines the position of the C2' / C3' atoms relative to the ribose plane. If"
" the C2' atom is above the plane, it is considered a C2'-endo conformation, "
"while if it is the C3' atom, it is a C3'-endo conformation (see figure taken"
" from [2](https://doi.org/10.3389/fgene.2022.95925). This property "
"correlates with the position of the 2'OH and its' interactions with "
"nucleobases, while also defining the RNA helix form."
msgstr ""
"もう1つは Sugar Puckering です。RNA の Ribose 平面に対し、C2' が上なら C2'-endo、C3' が上なら "
"C3'-endo です（[2](https://doi.org/10.3389/fgene.2022.95925) の図を参照）。2'OH の位置と "
"Nucleobase との相互作用に関係し、RNA Helix の形も決めます。"

#: README.md:71
msgid "<em>Representation of the C2' and C3' endo states.</em>"
msgstr "<em>C2'、C3' endo 状態。</em>"

#: README.md:74
msgid ""
"In MD simulations, the transitions between C2'/C3' endo and syn/anti states "
"can be difficult to converge, as slow degrees of freedom, therefore they are"
" good CV choices. The preparation of a CpH-Metadynamics simulation follows a"
" standard MD protocol: system setup, minimization, and initialization. "
"However, some considerations need to be addressed for the $\\chi$ OL3pH "
"force field (available [here](https://github.com/Tomfersil/CpH-"
"MetaD/tree/main/CpHMD_metaD/top/XOL3pH.ff))."
msgstr ""
"MD では C2'/C3' endo と syn/anti の遷移は遅く収束しにくいため、よい CV です。CpH-Metadynamics "
"の準備は通常の系設定・Minimization・初期化に従いますが、$\\chi$ OL3pH Force "
"Field（[こちら](https://github.com/Tomfersil/CpH-"
"MetaD/tree/main/CpHMD_metaD/top/XOL3pH.ff)）には注意点があります。"

#: README.md:76
msgid ""
"Our force field version was built in a modular approach compared to the "
"standard $\\chi$ OL3. As such, we need to convert the input .pdb file to be "
"compatible with the CpH nomenclature found in force field .rtp file. This "
"can be done manually or using the Python script available in the script "
"folder. The script converts and reorganizes the .pdb file, thus identifying "
"each ribose, phosphate group, nucleobase, and hydroxyl caps as independent "
"residues. After preparing the CpH-compatible .pdb file, then a standard MD "
"preparation protocol can be done before setting up the simulation."
msgstr ""
"この Force Field は標準 $\\chi$ OL3 と異なり Module 化されているため、入力 .pdb を .rtp の CpH "
"命名に合わせます。手動または scripts 内の Python で変換できます。スクリプトは各 "
"Ribose、Phosphate、Nucleobase、Hydroxyl Cap を独立残基として再構成します。CpH 対応 PDB の準備後は通常の "
"MD 準備を行えます。"

#: README.md:78
msgid "Setting up a CpH-Metadynamics simulation"
msgstr "CpH-Metadynamics の設定"

#: README.md:80
msgid ""
"Setting up a CpH-Metadynamics simulation requires defining parameters for "
"two sections: the CpHMD section and the PLUMED input file. Previous "
"knowledge on [metadynamics](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/advanced-methods.html) and/or CpHMD simulations is helpful. Examine"
" the CpHMD.settings file. For now, let's observe the main defining settings:"
msgstr ""
"CpHMD と PLUMED "
"入力の2部分を設定します。[Metadynamics](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/advanced-methods.html) や CpHMD の知識が役立ちます。CpHMD.settings の主な設定を見ます。"

#: README.md:101
msgid ""
"In this section, we need to define the number of segments and the size of "
"each segment in nanoseconds. In the following exercise, we will manage 100 "
"ns trajectories partitioned into 10 segments of 10 ns each. Another "
"important input is the choice of force field. Popular force fields were "
"specifically modified to incorporate multiple protonation tautomers for "
"different biomolecules (see: [CpHMD-v3.0 Github "
"page](https://github.com/NunoFBOliveira/CpHMD_v3/tree/main)). In this "
"tutorial, we will be studying a uridine nucleobase, so we will use the "
"XOL3pH ff (see the [XOL3pH "
"parametrization](https://github.com/Tomfersil/CpH-"
"MetaD/tree/main/CpHMD_metaD/top/XOL3pH.ff))."
msgstr ""
"Segment 数と各長さを ns で指定します。演習は100 ns を10 ns の10 Segment に分けます。Force Field "
"の選択も重要です。一般的なものを修正し、複数の Protonation Tautomer "
"に対応しています（[CpHMD-v3.0](https://github.com/NunoFBOliveira/CpHMD_v3/tree/main)）。Uridine"
" には XOL3pH を使います（[パラメータ化](https://github.com/Tomfersil/CpH-"
"MetaD/tree/main/CpHMD_metaD/top/XOL3pH.ff)）。"

#: README.md:103
msgid ""
"Then it is possible to choose either to perform a plain CpHMD simulation or "
"choose different options for a metadynamics simulation:"
msgstr "通常の CpHMD か、次の Metadynamics オプションを選べます。"

#: README.md:105
msgid ""
"plumed=yes: performs a metadynamics simulation reading from the HILLS every "
"cycle;"
msgstr "plumed=yes：Cycle ごとに HILLS を読み、Metadynamics を行う。"

#: README.md:106
msgid ""
"plumed=grid: stores both a GRID and HILLS file. Restarting a segment reads "
"from the GRIDS file. Recommended setting due to speed;"
msgstr "plumed=grid：GRID と HILLS を保存し、Segment 再開時は GRIDS を読む。高速なので推奨。"

#: README.md:107
msgid ""
"plumed=static: performs a static potential simulation by reading a previous "
"HILLS file. No more Gaussians are added and continue to explore the CV "
"space."
msgstr ""
"plumed=static：既存 HILLS の Static Potential を使う。Gaussian を追加せず CV 空間を探索する。"

#: README.md:109
msgid ""
"The \"sites=\" entry is needed to define the titrable sites based on the "
"residue numbering in the .pdb file used as input. It accepts either a number"
" or the all flag. Finally, we need to set system parameters such as the "
"simulation temperature, the pH, and the ionic strength (in mol/L) for the PB"
" calculations. For more details on the CpHMD settings, check the work done "
"by the Machuqueiro Lab in the previously linked GitHub pages."
msgstr ""
"「sites=」は入力 PDB の残基番号で Titration Site を指定し、数値または all を使えます。最後に、温度、pH、PB 計算の "
"Ionic Strength (mol/L) を設定します。詳細は上記の Machuqueiro Lab の GitHub を参照してください。"

#: README.md:111
msgid ""
"Concerning the specific parameters for the metadynamics section, either "
"check the end of the file or the template PLUMED_GRID.dat file. We recommend"
" this setting since it provides a greater advantage in I/O speed compared to"
" the HILLS file."
msgstr ""
"Metadynamics の詳細パラメータは末尾または PLUMED_GRID.dat を見ます。HILLS より I/O が速いため GRID "
"設定を推奨します。"

#: README.md:136
msgid ""
"The main argument is the METAD command. Using the ARG keyword we need to "
"specify the variables concerning our CVs upon the metadynamics bias will be "
"added. In the uridine system that we are studying, it will be the $\\chi$ "
"angle and ribose puckering. Then we need to define, for both CVs, the HEIGHT"
" of the Gaussians in kJ/mol, the width of the Gaussians defined by keyword "
"SIGMA, and the PACE (frequency in number of time steps) at which Gaussian "
"are added. The biasfactor and the temp are important parameters since they "
"will define the convergence of the initial barrier height scaling. The "
"defined parameters are standard for a nucleoside simulation using these "
"specific CVs."
msgstr ""
"主なコマンドは METAD で、ARG に Bias を加える CV を指定します。Uridine では $\\chi$ と Ribose "
"Puckering です。Gaussian 高さ HEIGHT (kJ/mol)、各 CV の幅 SIGMA、追加間隔 PACE（Time Step "
"数）を設定します。biasfactor と temp は初期 Barrier の Scale の収束を決める重要な値です。示す値はこの CV の "
"Nucleoside に標準的です。"

#: README.md:138
msgid ""
"Concerning the GRIDS, the bias potential is also written to a GRID file "
"(GRID_WFILE keyword) and then read (GRID_RFILE keyword) on the following "
"cycle. The grid boundaries are defined by GRID_MIN and GRID_MAX, while the "
"frequency of update is done every GRID_WSTRIDE time steps (it should match "
"the PACE)."
msgstr ""
"BiasPotential を GRID_WFILE で GRID に書き、次 Cycle に GRID_RFILE で読みます。範囲は "
"GRID_MIN・GRID_MAX、書き出し間隔は GRID_WSTRIDE で、PACE と合わせます。"

#: README.md:140
msgid ""
"After carefully choosing the PLUMED.dat parameters and the CpHMD settings, a"
" CpH-Metadynamics simulation can be run. To run a CpH-MetaD simulation, "
"there are available scripts and template settings files in the following "
"path of the [CpH-MetaD GitHub page](https://github.com/Tomfersil/CpH-"
"MetaD/blob/main/CpHMD_metaD/scripts/). These simulations will generate "
"several files:"
msgstr ""
"PLUMED.dat と CpHMD を適切に設定したら実行できます。[CpH-MetaD "
"GitHub](https://github.com/Tomfersil/CpH-"
"MetaD/blob/main/CpHMD_metaD/scripts/) にスクリプトと設定のひな形があります。次のファイルが生成されます。"

#: README.md:142
msgid "Simulation/Input data:"
msgstr "シミュレーション・入力データ："

#: README.md:143
msgid ""
"GRID: the GRID file that is necessary to restart each cycle and segment of "
"the CpH-MetaD. Do not erase between segments;"
msgstr "GRID：CpH-MetaD の各 Cycle・Segment の再開に必要。Segment 間で削除しない。"

#: README.md:144
msgid "HILLS: the accumulated bias potential of each segment ;"
msgstr "HILLS：各 Segment の蓄積 BiasPotential。"

#: README.md:145
msgid ".pHmdp: the general settings for each specific segment ;"
msgstr ".pHmdp：各 Segment の全般設定。"

#: README.md:146
msgid ""
".gro: the last frame of each .xtc segment is stored as a reference to start "
"the following segment ;"
